WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.350
You draw on the chart in true.

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.600
You steer by a compass.

3
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:13.100
Getting from one to the other is where more plotting-exam points are lost than anywhere else, and nearly always from one wrong sign.

4
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:15.375
Look at the chain on screen.

5
00:00:15.625 --> 00:00:19.475
True, variation, magnetic, deviation, compass.

6
00:00:19.725 --> 00:00:22.475
You met it in the Navigation module.

7
00:00:22.725 --> 00:00:28.050
Going down the chain, from true toward compass, you add west and subtract east.

8
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:33.575
Going up the chain, from compass toward true, you add east and subtract west.

9
00:00:34.575 --> 00:00:37.175
Now the advice that matters most.

10
00:00:37.425 --> 00:00:39.350
Don’t do this in your head.

11
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.925
Write every step on paper, one under the other, each with its sign.

12
00:00:44.175 --> 00:00:45.550
True.

13
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.500
Variation.

14
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.350
Magnetic.

15
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.300
Deviation.

16
00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.050
Compass.

17
00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:57.800
It takes ten seconds, and it’s the cheapest insurance on the exam.
